Subject: ps3av: mask the option bits off the mode in the audio setup

ps3av_set_audio_mode() looks up the current video mode's vid with
video_mode_table[ps3av->ps3av_mode], but ps3av_mode keeps the option
bits ps3fb passes with the mode (PS3AV_MODE_FULL 0x80, DVI 0x40, RGB
0x20 and the others). With any of them set, for example in the
full-screen modes (video=ps3fb:mode:133) or with a DVI monitor in auto
mode, the index runs past the 14-entry table. The vid read there is
then usually not a known one, ps3av_vid_video2av() maps it to 480p and
the HDMI audio N value is the 480p one for every mode.

Every other use masks the id first (ps3av_set_videomode_packet(),
ps3av_video_mode2res()); do the same here. ps3av_set_video_mode() and
the probe store only ids whose mode bits are in the table, so the mask
is enough.

Forwarded: no (an upstream bug; to send with a PS3 test)
---
 drivers/ps3/ps3av.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ps3/ps3av.c b/drivers/ps3/ps3av.c
--- a/drivers/ps3/ps3av.c
+++ b/drivers/ps3/ps3av.c
@@ -427,7 +427,7 @@ int ps3av_set_audio_mode(u32 ch, u32 fs,
 	avb_param.num_of_av_video_pkt = 0;
 	avb_param.num_of_av_audio_pkt = ps3av->av_hw_conf.num_of_hdmi;
 
-	vid = video_mode_table[ps3av->ps3av_mode].vid;
+	vid = video_mode_table[ps3av->ps3av_mode & PS3AV_MODE_MASK].vid;
 
 	/* audio mute */
 	ps3av_set_audio_mute(PS3AV_CMD_MUTE_ON);
